description: |
  Test results now hold their times as values instead of the text found
  in ``results.yaml``. Two things change in the output.

  A ``start-time`` or ``end-time`` given without a timezone is read as
  UTC and written back with the ``+00:00`` offset. Previously the string
  was stored and written out untouched. Values that already carry an
  offset are written back unchanged, and a value with whole seconds keeps
  exactly that precision.

  In the ``junit`` report, the ``time`` attribute is now emitted for a
  result whose duration was measured as zero. It used to be left out,
  which made a measured zero indistinguishable from a duration that was
  never measured. A duration that was never measured still has no
  ``time`` attribute.
